---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy" lang="en" description="How LISA Cloud and local Mac mode process accounts, conversations, and AI requests.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="rule"></span> PRIVACY <b>· updated 2026-09-27</b></p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      LISA is a personal AI assistant with two modes: <strong>LISA Cloud</strong>, operated
      by us, and a backend on <strong>your own Mac</strong>. Cloud mode processes and stores
      your account and assistant data. Local mode uses the server and AI providers you choose.
      We do not sell your personal data or use advertising tracking SDKs.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="highlight">
    <p class="eyebrow"><b>What we collect</b></p>
    <p class="big">Local mode: nothing — to us.</p>
    <p>
      Lisa Pocket and Lisa collect no analytics, no advertising identifiers, and contain no
      third-party tracking SDKs. Local mode does not require a LISA Cloud account. If you opt into a <strong>LISA Cloud account</strong>, we hold exactly
      what the section below lists — your email, your sign-in identifier, and your Lisa's
      data. You can request account deletion within the app.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="policy">
    <section class="pol">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>What stays on your device</b></p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Connection settings</strong> — the address of your backend and a device
          token are stored on your device (the iOS Keychain / app preferences) so the app can
          reconnect. The connection token is sent only to the backend it authenticates, including
          LISA Cloud when you choose cloud mode.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your conversations and Lisa’s memory (“soul”)</strong> live on the backend
          you connect to — your own Mac (under <code>~/.lisa</code>) or a Lisa Cloud instance
          you use. The app is a window onto that backend.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="pol">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>Your backend &amp; LLM providers</b></p>
      <p>
        When you chat, your messages are processed by the large-language-model provider
        configured on your backend (such as Anthropic, Zhipu/GLM, OpenAI, or Google).
        LISA Cloud relays requests using the service's configured providers; a local Mac uses
        your configuration. Relevant conversation history, memory, and tool results may be
        included with your message. The iOS app names the configured services and asks for
        permission before sending a chat message. Provider processing is governed by its own
        policy. A local model can keep inference on your Mac; local mode alone does not imply
        that a remote model never receives data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="pol">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>LISA Cloud accounts (optional)</b></p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>What we store</strong> — your email address, a sign-in identifier
          (Apple/Google <code>sub</code> or a password hash — never the password itself), and
          your Lisa's per-account home: her soul, your conversations, and anything you add to
          her knowledge base. Stored on Google Cloud (us-central1), isolated per account.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>What we process</strong> — chat messages pass through the account's metered
          LLM provider to answer you; token counts are metered for billing. We keep an
          append-only usage ledger (model, token counts, cost) — not message content.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sub-processors</strong> — LLM inference (e.g. Zhipu/GLM, Anthropic, OpenAI),
          Resend (verification &amp; sign-in code emails), Stripe (web top-ups), Apple
          (Sign in with Apple, iOS purchases), Google (Sign in with Google), Cloudflare
          (bot-check on signup). Each is governed by its own policy.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Deletion</strong> — "Delete account" in the app removes the account record
          and wipes the per-account home entirely; every session is invalidated at that
          instant. Payment transaction records used for deduplication and refunds are separate
          from conversation storage. Provider-side records and infrastructure backups follow
          their respective retention policies; contact us for a data request.
        </li>
        <li>
          The App Review demonstration account is shared with reviewers. Do not place personal
          information in that account. Ordinary cloud accounts have separate assistant data.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="pol">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>Notifications</b></p>
      <p>
        If you enable push notifications, a push token (Apple APNs, or an ntfy topic you choose)
        is used <em>only</em> to deliver the alerts you opt into, routed through the backend you
        paired with. It is not used for tracking.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="pol">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>Children</b></p>
      <p>Lisa is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect their data.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="pol">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>Changes</b></p>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the apps evolve; material changes will be noted here with a
        new date. The source is public:
        <a href="https://github.com/oratis/LISA">github.com/oratis/LISA</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="pol">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>Contact</b></p>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy? Open an issue at
        <a href="https://github.com/oratis/LISA/issues">github.com/oratis/LISA/issues</a>
        or email <a href="mailto:wangharp@gmail.com">wangharp@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <style>
    .page-head h1 { margin-bottom: .4rem; }
    .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--muted); max-width: 68ch; }

    .highlight {
      margin: 2.2rem 0 0; background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--panel), var(--bg-elev));
      border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 3px solid var(--good);
      border-radius: 14px; padding: 1.3rem 1.5rem;
    }
    .highlight .eyebrow { margin-bottom: .5rem; }
    .highlight .big {
      font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.55rem;
      color: var(--ink); margin: 0 0 .5rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }
    .highlight p:last-child { margin: 0; max-width: 70ch; }

    .policy { display: grid; gap: 2rem; margin-top: 2.2rem; }
    .pol .eyebrow { margin-bottom: .5rem; }
    .pol p { margin: 0; max-width: 72ch; }
    .pol ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; max-width: 72ch; }
    .pol li { margin: .5rem 0; color: var(--muted); }
    .pol li strong { color: var(--ink); }
  </style>
</Base>
